##
## smem.soar — SMEM initialization and CQ-ISC loading rules
## Spec 008: SOAR-Powered Claude Code Software Development Agent
## Version: 1.0.0
##
## INV-001: chunk never inherited from codegen.soar (parent sources this file)
## INV-002: CQ-ISC prohibit preferences are the SOLE enforcement mechanism.
## INV-005: (build ^current-phase <phase>) MUST be FIRST LHS condition.
##
## SMEM namespace: ^ns cq-isc  (quality rule corpus)
##                 ^ns advisory (IMPLEMENTER best-preference staging)
##

##
## SMEM: Initialize quality rule namespace
##

smem --add {
  (<ns-cq-isc>
    ^ns cq-isc
    ^description |CQ-ISC library namespace: Code Quality Impossibility Constraints|
    ^version |1.0.0|
    ^schema-version |cq-isc-schema-v1.0.0|
    ^loaded-count 0
    ^quarantine-count 0)
}

smem --add {
  (<ns-advisory>
    ^ns advisory
    ^description |IMPLEMENTER advisory namespace: best-preference staging area (INV-003)|
    ^version |1.0.0|)
}

smem --add {
  (<quarantine>
    ^ns cq-isc-quarantine
    ^description |Entries that failed Executor validation — do NOT fire prohibit preferences|)
}

##
## SMEM: Load CQ-ISC entries from default library
## The smem_loader.py script populates SMEM at pipeline start via SML API.
## These production rules handle the SMEM retrieval and WM activation.
##

sp {codegen*smem*init-load-cq-isc-library
  (state <s> ^name codegen
             ^build <b>)
  (<b> ^current-phase RE   ;; INV-005
       ^cq-isc-library-loaded false)
  -->
  (<s> ^operator <o> + >)
  (<o> ^name load-cq-isc-from-smem)
  (write (crlf) |[SOAR SMEM] Initiating CQ-ISC library load from SMEM|)
}

## DISABLED: <cq-entry> is unbound on LHS — causes "ungrounded variable" source error.
## CQ-ISC violations are injected directly by ViolationScanner → SOARBridge (Python).
## Re-enable when SMEM dynamic loading is implemented via SML API.
##
## sp {codegen*smem*apply-load-cq-isc-library
##   (state <s> ^name codegen
##              ^operator <o>)
##   (<o> ^name load-cq-isc-from-smem)
##   (<s> ^build <b>)
##   -->
##   (<b> ^cq-isc-library-loaded true)
##   (smem --retrieve <cq-entry>)
##   (<cq-entry> ^ns cq-isc
##               ^policy-drift-status current)
##   (write (crlf) |[SOAR SMEM] CQ-ISC library load request submitted|)
## }

##
## SMEM: Retrieve individual CQ-ISC entry and instantiate prohibit production rule
## For each non-drifted entry retrieved from SMEM, activate it in Working Memory.
##

## DISABLED: (smem <mem> ^...) is not valid SOAR LHS condition syntax.
## SMEM queries use smem --query on RHS or (<s> ^smem <smem>) (<smem> ^retrieved <r>).
##
## sp {codegen*smem*activate-cq-isc-entry
##   ...
## }

##
## SMEM: Policy drift detection
## If a CQ-ISC entry's source constitution section has changed,
## it is marked drifted and EXCLUDED from prohibit preference evaluation.
##

## DISABLED: invalid (smem <mem> ^...) LHS condition syntax — see note above.
##
## sp {codegen*smem*detect-policy-drift ... }
## sp {codegen*smem*quarantine-drifted-entry ... }

##
## SMEM: Quarantine mechanism
## Entries in pending-validation do NOT fire prohibit preferences.
##

## DISABLED: invalid (smem <mem> ^...) LHS condition syntax — see note above.
##
## sp {codegen*smem*quarantine-pending-validation ... }

##
## SMEM: Advisory namespace management (INV-003)
## IMPLEMENTER outputs are staged here as best preferences.
## These NEVER override prohibit preferences.
##

## DISABLED: (<conf> >= 0.5) is old comparison syntax (needs {<conf> >= 0.5}).
## Also uses (implementer-output <io> ^...) which is not a valid state-linked WME.
##
## sp {codegen*smem*stage-implementer-advisory ... }

##
## SMEM: CQ-ISC prohibit preference generation template
## One rule per CQ-ISC entry, generated by smem_loader.py via SML.
## INV-005 enforced: (build ^current-phase <phase>) MUST be FIRST LHS condition.
## INV-002 enforced: prohibit preference is the SOLE enforcement mechanism.
##
## Template instantiation (done by smem_loader.py):
##
## sp {cq-isc*CQ-ISC-SEC-001*prohibit
##   (state <s> ^name codegen)
##   (build <b> ^current-phase GATE)                   ;; INV-005 — FIRST
##   (code-violation <v> ^cq-isc-id |CQ-ISC-SEC-001|
##                       ^status confirmed-failing)
##   -->
##   (<s> ^operator <o> - :prohibit)                   ;; INV-002 — SOLE mechanism
##   (epmem --add <e>)
##   (<e> ^cq-isc-fired |CQ-ISC-SEC-001|)
## }
##
## The smem_loader.py script generates one sp block per CQ-ISC entry
## and loads it via SML kernel.LoadSoarFile() or kernel.ExecuteCommandLine().
##

##
## SMEM: Record SMEM state for EPMEM audit (INV-004)
##

## DISABLED: (epmem --add <audit>) with unbound <audit> causes "ungrounded variable" error.
## SOAR 9.6.4 automatic episodic recording captures this transition implicitly (INV-004).
##
## sp {codegen*smem*record-load-complete ... }
